WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:10.280
The secure SDLC integrates security into planning, requirements, design, development, testing, release, operations, and maintenance.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.660
It moves security from a late surprise to a normal part of engineering practice.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:24.000
That shift matters because early decisions shape architecture, data flows, dependencies, controls, testing strategy, and operational visibility.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:37.100
Strong programs combine secure requirements, threat modeling, secure design, secure coding, dependency governance, security testing, pipeline controls, release discipline, and vulnerability response.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.640
No single activity is enough by itself.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:42.420
Requirements tell teams what must be protected.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.040
Threat modeling reveals design risks.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.500
Coding practices implement the controls.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.200
Testing verifies selected assumptions.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.060
Operations feedback keeps the loop alive.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:01:00.320
Security is shared across product, engineering, QA, operations, security, compliance, and leadership.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:04.060
Product teams help define acceptable risk and user impact.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.760
Engineers design and build controls.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.900
QA verifies behavior.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.280
Operations monitors and responds.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.580
Security teams guide risk and review.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.080
Compliance teams help align evidence with obligations.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.940
Leaders make tradeoffs visible and fund the work.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.080
The goal is not perfect software.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.060
The goal is repeatable, evidence-backed risk reduction throughout the lifecycle.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:35.000
A mature secure SDLC helps teams make better decisions, respond faster, avoid recurring mistakes, and build software that customers and operators can trust.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.260
It is practical engineering discipline applied continuously.
